ndrome. II. Physiological correlations and definition of an ARDS Severity Score. CT Scan ARDS Study Group</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2000</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>1046</fpage><lpage>1056</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11030160</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s001340051317</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mayo</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Aldrich</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>NL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Radiation exposure at chest CT: a statement of the Fleischner Society</article-title><source>Radiology</source><year>2003</year><volume>228</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12832569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Beckmann</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillies</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Berenholtz</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wu</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Pronovost</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Incidents relating to the intra-hospital transfer of critically ill patients. An analysis of the reports submitted to the Australian Incident Monitoring Study in Intensive Care</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2004</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1579</fpage><lpage>1585</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14991102</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00134-004-2177-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kirkpatrick</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Breeck</surname><given-names>K</given-n